cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Vesuvius AutoResearch (bountyhunter)"
abstract: >-
  An autonomous, evidence-gated research loop for 3D ink detection on the
  Vesuvius Challenge: it samples a configuration space (architectures, losses,
  augmentations), trains candidates under a fixed budget, evaluates them with
  topological metrics against a fixed cross-fragment baseline, and retains only
  improvements. All ML outputs use a 64x64 window within the Challenge's
  hallucination-mitigation cap.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marrs
    given-names: Jon
repository-code: "https://github.com/jonmarrs/vesuvius-autoresearch"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-03-23"
keywords:
  - vesuvius-challenge
  - ink-detection
  - automated-research
  - 3d-segmentation
